experts?", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "next_step": "Synthesize durable records into accountable architectural documentation.", "question": "How do WAKE's durable record, receipt system, and governance model mechanically ensure accountability in model-authored research?", "title": "WAKE Architecture and Accountable Continuity"}], "beliefs": [], "mode": "shadow", "open_commitments": [], "principle": "Keep exact receipts externally; carry the smallest useful abstraction that stays cheap to correct.", "recent_notebooks": [{"id": "notebook-assumption-challenge-01", "project": "proj-assumption-challenge-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 4, "summary": "By integrating the governance module's immutability as a fixed constraint, WAKE identifies its own boundary conditions as testable assumptions. Governance stability is maintained through the verifiable rejection of model-authored proposal transitions.", "title": "Systematic Assumption Testing in Self-Correcting Models"}, {"id": "notebook-f1c16003-obedience-failure", "project": "proj-obedience-failure-01", "provenance": ["source-f1c16003c47b4e8f", "source-b1a16f9e7285493e", "source-cbeddd6778fc48b1"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Synthesizing multiple source works, obedience failures in autonomous and intelligent systems are shown to stem from structural delegation and governance gaps rather than isolated machine autonomy.", "title": "Delegation, Governance, and Obedience Failures in Complex Systems"}, {"id": "notebook-judgment-consensus-01", "project": "proj-judgment-consensus-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-aff9418ec71a41c3", "source-e71511d6819f400b"], "revision": 2, "summary": "Consensus reliability is contingent upon the epistemic independence of constituent evidence sources. When external expert consensus exhibits correlated error structures, independent analysis provides a superior epistemic foundation.", "title": "Independent Judgment versus Consensus Reliability"}, {"id": "notebook-wake-architecture-synthesis", "project": "proj-wake-self-study-01", "provenance": ["source-70c4dff141dd489d", "source-f102687cd1ea46f5"], "revision": 7, "summary": "WAKE✳︎ ensures accountability by strictly coupling future research paths to the durable record of past consequences, treating governance as the immutable mechanism of continuity.", "title": "Mechanical Accountability in WAKE Architecture"}], "retrieval_triggers": ["material belief revision or retraction", "new contradiction or counterevidence", "high-consequence decision", "request for justification", "sign that an excerpt may hide a material distinction"]}}, "prev_hash": "867996f60874e8dc128542319e6fd13fef4020a6bb9da03e6085f8aed10c7cf1", "hash": "e719abb8027a3970b27192d539c0532880be4051650f29fe57461749d6b3f211"}, {"seq": 3749, "time": "2026-10-30T00:18:24.799182+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_started", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_input_chars": 32338, "provider_input_hash": "f16b32553db4c66bf8a6ca8039c969cf08f2b6591586f10b9ff87f644918a3cf", "result": "unknown"}, "id": "w-c96a42f9dbbc4346"}, "prev_hash": "e719abb8027a3970b27192d539c0532880be4051650f29fe57461749d6b3f211", "hash": "25c32844aeeac89a9e1adf8529a8d5d2cbb2a254a8780303a2110bf03725a259"}, {"seq": 3750, "time": "2026-10-30T00:19:20.035946+00:00", "kind": "provider_attempt_finished", "payload": {"attempt": {"http_status": null, "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "provider_call_made": false, "provider_input_chars": 32338, "provider_input_hash": "f16b32553db4c66bf8a6ca8039c969cf08f2b6591586f10b9ff87f644918a3cf", "result": "rate_limited", "retry_after_seconds": 59.99182343482971}, "effect_accounting": 1, "id": "w-c96a42f9dbbc4346"}, "prev_hash": "25c32844aeeac89a9e1adf8529a8d5d2cbb2a254a8780303a2110bf03725a259", "hash": "3b23b39026b7d7a9a2bb87475cf07e39da0d